ing the turn) could mean either weakness OR a trap with a strong hand. A value bet risks getting raised by better hands (any King, better Queens, or two pair), while worse hands will likely just fold. Checking allows me to see showdown without additional risk. My pair of Queens has showdown value against missed draws and smaller pairs, which is what the opponent's checking pattern suggests they might hold.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
